# =============================================================================
# WashU SHPE — environment configuration
# Copy to `.env.local` and fill in. `.env.local` is git-ignored.
# =============================================================================
#
# ANYTHING PREFIXED `VITE_` IS COMPILED INTO THE BROWSER BUNDLE AND IS PUBLIC.
# Never put a secret behind a VITE_ prefix.
#
# The Supabase *anon* key below is designed to be public — it identifies the
# project, it does not authorise anything. All access control comes from
# Supabase Auth + Row Level Security. The *service role* key is the opposite:
# it bypasses RLS entirely and must never reach the browser.
# =============================================================================

# ── Supabase (required for the member portal) ───────────────────────────────
# Project Settings → API in the Supabase dashboard.
# Leave blank to run the public marketing site only; the portal will render a
# clear "not configured" notice instead of crashing.
VITE_SUPABASE_URL=
VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=

# ── Deployment base path ────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Defaults to "/" for Netlify, which is production. Set it to a sub-path such
# as "/SHPE_Website/" only if you are publishing to a static host that serves
# the site from a folder. Consumed by vite.config.ts → import.meta.env.BASE_URL,
# which drives both asset URLs and the React Router basename.
VITE_BASE_PATH=/

# ── Canonical site URL ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Used to build Supabase auth redirect targets (email confirmation, password
# reset). Must exactly match one of the Redirect URLs allow-listed under
# Supabase → Authentication → URL Configuration.
#
# It is also the origin of every business-card URL the app produces: the
# address written to NFC chips, QR codes, the share link and the officers'
# NFC programming sheet. Locally that is harmless. On Netlify it must be the
# production origin (https://washushpe.org) in EVERY deploy context, deploy
# previews included: a chip written from a preview with the preview's own
# address stops working the day the preview is deleted, and a chip can't be
# fixed without rewriting it by hand.
VITE_SITE_URL=http://localhost:5173

# ── Registration policy (client-side UX only) ───────────────────────────────
# Comma-separated. The authoritative check lives in the database
# (`public.enforce_signup_email_domain` + the `allowed_email_domains` row in
# `app_settings`); this copy exists so the form can fail fast with a good
# message. Changing this alone does NOT weaken enforcement.
VITE_ALLOWED_EMAIL_DOMAINS=wustl.edu

# =============================================================================
# NETLIFY FUNCTIONS — keep-supabase-awake, admin-password-reset-link and the
# card-meta edge function
# =============================================================================
# All three read VITE_SUPABASE_URL and VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY at runtime;
# admin-password-reset-link and the edge function also read VITE_SITE_URL.
# (The fourth function, netlify/functions/health, reads nothing.) Nothing new
# to add locally. On Netlify, those variables must be set in the UI, because
# values set in netlify.toml reach the build only, never functions or edge
# functions. On a plan with scopes, include the "Functions" scope ("All
# scopes", the default, does); on a plan without them, every variable already
# reaches functions.
#
# Optional fallbacks, read only when the VITE_ names are not available to the
# Functions scope. Same public values; never the service role key.
# SUPABASE_URL=
# SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=
# SITE_URL=

# =============================================================================
# SERVER-SIDE ONLY — never prefixed with VITE_, never committed.
# =============================================================================
# The service role key bypasses Row Level Security entirely. Exactly one
# shipped file reads it: netlify/functions/admin-password-reset-link.ts, which
# uses it to ask Supabase Auth for a member's password reset link, and only
# after the database has confirmed the caller is an admin.
#
# On Netlify: Site configuration → Environment variables. Tick "Contains
# secret values", and give it a value for the Production deploy context only:
# a deploy preview or branch deploy runs a branch's code, functions included,
# before anyone has reviewed it.
#
# If the site's plan offers scopes, give it the "Functions" scope only (not
# Builds, not "All scopes"), which keeps it out of the build. Not every plan
# offers them, and on one without scopes the key is visible to builds as well,
# so anything that runs during a build, a build plugin included, could read
# it: don't add build plugins you don't trust. Either way the function's own
# code has the key while it runs, which is why only reviewed code, the
# Production context, should get a value.
#
# Functions read environment variables as of their deploy. After adding or
# changing the key, trigger a new deploy (Deploys → Trigger deploy) before
# expecting a reset link to work. Without the key, everything else still
# works; creating a reset link from a member's Administration tab just says it
# isn't set up.
#
# Never VITE_SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY: a VITE_ prefix would compile the key
# into the public bundle.
#
# Not needed for local development, and never paste the production key into
# a file. Under `npm run dev` the function doesn't run, so the Administration
# tab says reset links aren't available here. `netlify dev` doesn't change
# that in a browser: it applies netlify.toml's production CSP to the pages it
# serves, which blocks the inline preamble Vite's React plugin injects and a
# local Supabase on http://127.0.0.1:54321. What does run locally are the
# tests: the function's behaviour is covered by
# src/services/__tests__/adminPasswordResetLinkFunction.test.ts (`npm test`)
# and its SQL by supabase/tests/password_reset_links.test.sql
# (`npm run db:test`). Try the whole flow on the production site, the one
# deploy context that has the key.
# SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=
